1
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:09,134
[phone ringing]

2
00:00:17,059 --> 00:00:19,560
JIN LAI HAO - CLOSED

3
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:21,313
[phone continues ringing]

4
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:30,197
[Chien-yuan] <i>Yes.</i>

5
00:00:30,322 --> 00:00:31,782
<i>I did kill your dad.</i>

6
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:35,077
- [tires screeching]
- [engine revving]

7
00:00:37,496 --> 00:00:38,539
Chou jin-lai!

8
00:00:38,664 --> 00:00:39,872
[horn honking]

9
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:41,040
Stop!

10
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,793
[phone ringing]

11
00:00:43,043 --> 00:00:44,586
[Chien-yuan]
<i>And I think he deserved it.</i>

12
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:48,506
[tires screeching]

13
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:49,591
[car crash]

14
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:54,262
<i>If he had listened to me,
he wouldn't have died.</i>

15
00:00:54,263 --> 00:00:55,513
[phone ringing]

16
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:58,182
<i>If he didn't die,
you wouldn't have been in jail.</i>

17
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,851
HANDSOME BOY

18
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:04,314
[Chien-yuan] <i>The one
who put you in this pathetic
life is not me,</i>

19
00:01:08,277 --> 00:01:09,319
but your dad.

20
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:12,531
[tense music playing]

21
00:01:18,704 --> 00:01:19,538
What?

22
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:21,707
Wanna hit me?

23
00:01:23,709 --> 00:01:24,875
Fine.

24
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:25,877
Come on.

25
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:27,921
Hit me.

26
00:01:29,089 --> 00:01:30,798
Do it.

27
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:31,800
Do it now.

28
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,261
Do it.

29
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:35,887
Do what you like to do the most.

30
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:40,309
Let go!

31
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:42,394
I've tolerated you
for ten years.

32
00:01:43,395 --> 00:01:45,230
I can do it for another 20.

33
00:01:45,856 --> 00:01:47,107
What are you talking about?

34
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:48,692
Your statute of limitations.

35
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:52,696
By then, I'll show you
how patient I can be.

36
00:01:57,409 --> 00:01:59,119
Damn! What are you doing?

37
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:00,828
You wanna fight?

38
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,539
I'll fight you. Come on!

39
00:02:06,293 --> 00:02:07,753
You pathetic coward.

40
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:10,755
Isn't he your high school mate?

41
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:12,257
[Chien-yuan] What mate?

42
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:15,135
On his first day at school,
I got him expelled.

43
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,303
Loser.

44
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:17,471
[Chien-yuan's friend]
What did he say?

45
00:02:17,596 --> 00:02:19,806
Statute of limitations?
What's that about?

46
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:21,557
It's not important.

47
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:24,311
[Chien-yuan's friend] Alright,
let's go have a smoke. Come on.

48
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:26,480
Come on. Wait for me.

49
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,359
[singer] <i>♪ Someday ♪</i>

50
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:33,654
<i>♪ You can find sunshine,
sunshine ♪</i>

51
00:02:33,779 --> 00:02:38,616
[singing in Mandarin]

52
00:02:38,617 --> 00:02:40,660
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

53
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:42,828
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

54
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:44,831
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

55
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:47,249
[singing in Mandarin]

56
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:51,171
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

57
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:55,717
[singing foreign language]

58
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,682
[dramatic music playing]

59
00:03:02,683 --> 00:03:04,226
[ambient street noise]

60
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:30,669
[music continues]

61
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:49,521
There will be many VVIPs
this evening.
This is a TV journalist.

62
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,897
Don't put them with the KOLs.
They'll be in the private rooms.

63
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:54,859
<i>They all have their photos,
so don't get mixed up.</i>

64
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,027
[restaurant worker] <i>Understood.</i>

65
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:59,698
GRAND OPENING
OF JIN LAI XUAN
FLAGSHIP RESTAURANT

66
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:03,201
<i>Hi, guys,
Qian-qian reporting live.</i>

67
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:05,537
<i>Today I'm invited
to the opening</i>

68
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:08,206
<i>of Chang Xin Group's
flagship restaurant.</i>

69
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:09,875
<i>As you know, Chang Xin's
a large conglomerate.</i>

70
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,919
<i>They own restaurants,
logistics... I can't
remember them all.</i>

71
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:16,757
<i>But being in logistics
means having
the freshest ingredients.</i>

72
00:04:17,299 --> 00:04:19,426
I wonder what great food
we're having today.

73
00:04:19,551 --> 00:04:21,928
I think I just saw
Chang Xin's heir walk past.

74
00:04:24,473 --> 00:04:27,058
Hsiu-wen, you good?
Need my help?

75
00:04:27,309 --> 00:04:29,269
[Hsiu-wen] Find something to do
if you're free.

76
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:31,812
I'm busy.

77
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:34,732
Ms. Hsiu-wen?
There's been an accident
in the parking lot.

78
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:36,776
Some media can't get in.
They'll be late.

79
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:38,569
- Has it been sorted?
- [worker] Yes, we're on it.

80
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:40,906
Well, you don't have
to worry about that.
I've dealt with it.

81
00:04:41,031 --> 00:04:43,365
You dealt with it? How?

82
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:45,285
I called headquarters
to send someone over.

83
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:50,998
Get some more snow fungus soup
for the journalists,

84
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:52,042
and some coupons too.

85
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,752
- Okay.
- Thank you.

86
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:55,420
You called the head office?

87
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:58,799
[sighs] No biggie.

88
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:00,258
We're busy.

89
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:01,927
They will understand.

90
00:05:02,052 --> 00:05:03,469
Here.

91
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:04,637
I'm really busy.

92
00:05:04,638 --> 00:05:06,640
I have to introduce
our new set menus later.

93
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:11,394
[dramatic music playing]

94
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:17,442
[music intensifies]

95
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,664
[cameras clicking]

96
00:05:30,789 --> 00:05:34,000
JIN LAI XUAN - GRAND OPENING

97
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:41,424
[indistinct chatter]

98
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:46,972
[glasses clink]

99
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:48,931
[Shu-min] Mr. Chairman.

100
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:50,475
- Shu-min.
- [Shu-min] Director Chiang.

101
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,893
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

102
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:55,647
The interior looks elegant.
The dishes look good too.

103
00:05:56,815 --> 00:06:00,694
All thanks to Hsiu-wen.
She's of great help.

104
00:06:00,819 --> 00:06:01,987
No wonder she's your favorite.

105
00:06:02,112 --> 00:06:02,988
[chuckles]

106
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:05,490
Chien-yuen helped a lot, too.

107
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:09,494
You guys are
the upcoming generation
of the company.

108
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:12,372
Good job.
You can handle things
on your own now.

109
00:06:13,999 --> 00:06:15,875
Hsiu-wen is really good.

110
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:17,669
She reminds me of you
when you were younger.

111
00:06:19,504 --> 00:06:20,422
As for Chien-yuen,

112
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:22,465
he's still too green.

113
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:35,020
[sighs] What were you thinking?

114
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:38,690
How old are you?

115
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:41,526
Do what you think is right.

116
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:44,945
Hsiu-wen has already
sorted everything for you.

117
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:46,031
Aren't you embarrassed?

118
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:49,618
[sighs]

119
00:06:52,704 --> 00:06:53,705
[sighs]

120
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:57,083
Step back from everything
related to Jin Lai Xuan
from now on.

121
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:58,877
Hsiu-wen will take over.

122
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:02,547
- But, Dad...
- What?

123
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:04,549
Got a problem?

124
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:09,137
No.

125
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:13,808
Then what are you
standing there for?
Got nothing to do? Huh?

126
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:25,069
- [sighs]
- [door opens]

127
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:27,072
[indistinct chatter]

128
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:31,701
[Chang Ta-chin grunts]

129
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:35,622
Mr. Chairman?

130
00:07:35,747 --> 00:07:37,164
Yushan Hall is ready.

131
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:39,250
Here's the guest list
for dinner.

132
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:41,795
- You can check the seating.
- Okay.

133
00:07:44,923 --> 00:07:46,131
Good.

134
00:07:46,132 --> 00:07:47,801
By the way,

135
00:07:47,926 --> 00:07:50,886
I heard Chou Jin-lai's son
owns a restaurant around here.

136
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:51,930
Did you know?

137
00:07:53,264 --> 00:07:54,181
I do.

138
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:56,059
Why didn't you tell me?

139
00:07:56,935 --> 00:07:59,771
[tense music playing]

140
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,108
JIN LAI HAO

141
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:13,910
I think...

142
00:08:14,619 --> 00:08:16,997
it's a small restaurant
without much potential

143
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:18,623
that you don't need
to concern yourself with.

144
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:22,502
[chuckles]

145
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:23,461
That's true.

146
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:30,176
If things happened
like ten years ago,

147
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:33,138
and I made the exact same offer
to sponsor your family,

148
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:35,807
who would you choose?

149
00:08:40,812 --> 00:08:42,564
[soft chuckle]

150
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:46,484
I've always belonged
to Chang Xin.

151
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:49,654
So I'm not sure
what you mean, sir.

152
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:58,621
[laughs]

153
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:03,835
This is why I like you.

154
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:09,841
But if you mind his restaurant,
I can sort it out.

155
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:11,676
It's fine.

156
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:13,053
Go get busy.

157
00:09:22,187 --> 00:09:24,189
- [door opens]
- [indistinct chatter]

158
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:27,025
[door closes]

159
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:29,235
[Chang Ta-chin]
<i>Taiwanese cuisine
is our foundation.</i>

160
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,861
[cameras clicking]

161
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,197
<i>Continuing the legacy
is our motto.</i>

162
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:37,827
<i>Our brand's culture
will be the DNA
to build our next 30 years on.</i>

163
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:41,206
We continue to optimize
the standards of our operations.

164
00:09:42,123 --> 00:09:45,335
<i>We replace laborious tasks
with machine automation</i>

165
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:49,881
<i>and combine data with AI
to find the most loved
Taiwanese dishes.</i>

166
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:53,258
<i>We only keep the dishes
that best suit our customers.</i>

167
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:54,802
[dramatic music playing]

168
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:58,723
<i>To make Taiwanese dishes
go international</i>

169
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:03,143
henceforth, we will
work together
with Ding Xiong Construction

170
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,354
and Da Fa Engineering.

171
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:06,231
We will start
with the end in mind,

172
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:07,649
<i>hold on to our beliefs,</i>

173
00:10:09,234 --> 00:10:12,612
and together drive
the mission of reviving
Taiwanese banquet cuisine.

174
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:13,738
- [laughs]
- [thuds]

175
00:10:14,906 --> 00:10:16,074
[Chang Ta-chin]
<i>Today, we are presenting</i>

176
00:10:16,199 --> 00:10:18,618
a new brand of adapting
classic banquet dishes,

177
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:19,786
Jin Lai Xuan.

178
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,121
[thudding]

179
00:10:21,913 --> 00:10:24,165
[dramatic music playing]

180
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:25,917
[loud thud]

181
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:31,046
CHANG XIN - CHANG CHIEN-YUEN

182
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,256
SCHOOL VIOLENCE

183
00:10:32,257 --> 00:10:33,799
CHANG CHIEN-YUEN,
HEIR OF CHANG XIN GROUP

184
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,635
THE SUSPECT IS
A STUDENT NAMED CHOU

185
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:36,761
THE INCIDENT OCCURRED ON CAMPUS

186
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,429
ASSAULT INCIDENT

187
00:10:40,849 --> 00:10:41,932
CHOU LU-YUNG

188
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:46,688
JIN LAI HAO TAIWANESE CUISINE

189
00:10:48,398 --> 00:10:49,356
REVIEWS: 3.5 STARS

190
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:50,400
WORST SERVICE ATTITUDE

191
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:52,277
BEST FOOD, WORST SERVICE

192
00:10:53,111 --> 00:10:54,946
[indistinct chatter]

193
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:00,785
[Yi-hsuan] It's cute!

194
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:04,037
<i>Where have
I tasted this before?</i>

195
00:11:04,038 --> 00:11:05,957
[emotional music playing]

196
00:11:09,961 --> 00:11:11,754
<i>I don't remember anything
from before I was ten.</i>

197
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:14,966
<i>But this taste is so familiar.</i>

198
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:16,926
<i>Why?</i>

199
00:11:17,969 --> 00:11:19,804
<i>How can a complete stranger...</i>

200
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:23,141
<i>make a familiar taste
like this?</i>

201
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:27,770
[deep breath]

202
00:11:38,448 --> 00:11:42,869
JIN LAI HAO

203
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:52,003
[door opens]

204
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:55,215
[Chin-nan]
You said nobody is coming?
Someone's here.

205
00:11:56,925 --> 00:11:58,843
Welcome. Dining here?

206
00:11:59,719 --> 00:12:01,261
[Hsiu-wen] Is Chou Lu-yung here?

207
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,804
Boss?

208
00:12:02,805 --> 00:12:04,891
- Someone's here for you.
- Why are you here?

209
00:12:05,016 --> 00:12:06,392
I wanted to take a look.
Can't I?

210
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:10,354
You can.

211
00:12:10,355 --> 00:12:13,233
I'm heading back to office soon.
Just wanted
to see if you're here.

212
00:12:16,027 --> 00:12:17,904
This is my good friend,
Hsiu-wen.

213
00:12:18,029 --> 00:12:18,863
My co-worker.

214
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:23,201
Lin Chin-nan.
I'm the pride of Jin Lai.

215
00:12:25,662 --> 00:12:26,496
Hello.

216
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:32,043
The place's not big.
Want me to show you around?

217
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:33,044
Sure.

218
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:42,345
I have two co-workers,
one front-of-house
and one back-of-house.

219
00:12:42,971 --> 00:12:44,222
This is Yu-li.

220
00:12:49,852 --> 00:12:51,104
The space is just right.

221
00:12:57,402 --> 00:12:58,820
Do you still have
milkfish congee?

222
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:01,072
Yeah.

223
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:04,324
[soft chuckles]

224
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:05,576
[electronic dings]

225
00:13:07,078 --> 00:13:08,204
[store clerk]
Just a moment for the receipt.

226
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:12,291
Give me that. Give me that.

227
00:13:12,292 --> 00:13:14,126
Give me! Give me that.

228
00:13:14,127 --> 00:13:15,419
Thank you. Give me that.

229
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:16,546
[cashier] What's wrong with him?

230
00:13:16,796 --> 00:13:18,214
[old man]
Nobody wants this, right?

231
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:19,924
Excuse me.

232
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:22,342
Please don't ask our customers
for their receipts.

233
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:24,261
But they don't want them.

234
00:13:24,262 --> 00:13:27,097
I've told you.
If you want them,
ask for them outside.

235
00:13:27,098 --> 00:13:28,099
Give it to me.

236
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:30,183
But Miss...

237
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:31,184
- No.
- What are you doing?

238
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:32,437
- Don't do this.
- Don't grab me.

239
00:13:32,562 --> 00:13:33,771
- Can you let go?
- Show me some mercy.

240
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:35,939
What are you doing?
Don't do this.

241
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:38,276
[screaming]

242
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,823
Are you okay, sir?

243
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:45,324
I'm okay.

244
00:13:45,325 --> 00:13:47,201
- I was pushed...
- [scoffs]

245
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:51,330
How can you bully an old man?

246
00:13:51,331 --> 00:13:53,124
He grabbed me first,
just like you're doing now.

247
00:13:54,292 --> 00:13:55,209
Oh.

248
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:56,836
I'm sorry.

249
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:58,421
But you can't push an old man.

250
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:02,592
[stammers] It's okay.

251
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:06,011
I'm kind-hearted.
I'll forgive you.

252
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:08,014
[light music playing]

253
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:11,559
Are you happy
that you've done good?

254
00:14:15,313 --> 00:14:16,647
Are you going
to Grand Guanyin Temple?

255
00:14:16,898 --> 00:14:18,106
Grand Guanyin Temple?

256
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:19,984
The oldest Guanyin temple
in Tainan.

257
00:14:20,443 --> 00:14:24,404
Oh. Oh, I'm not a tourist.
I just moved here.

258
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:26,323
Then you should
visit the temple.

259
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:28,868
You'll like it there.
You're like Guanyin,
always there to help.

260
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:30,995
[bell tolls]

261
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:34,540
I didn't push him.

262
00:14:39,504 --> 00:14:41,089
[electronic dings]

263
00:14:47,345 --> 00:14:48,388
[grunts]

264
00:14:49,389 --> 00:14:51,933
Weren't you getting water?
Where is it?

265
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:56,521
I'm not thirsty anymore.

266
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:02,026
[Chin-lai] How's that?

267
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:03,569
You remember our old house?

268
00:15:04,529 --> 00:15:06,114
[Lu-yung] It seems smaller now.

269
00:15:06,531 --> 00:15:08,199
[Chin-lai]
That's because you've grown up.

270
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,034
You good?

271
00:15:13,413 --> 00:15:15,081
Lots to clean up.

272
00:15:15,206 --> 00:15:17,583
We'll take our time. No rush.

273
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:18,918
I'm going to cook something.

274
00:15:19,544 --> 00:15:20,378
But I'm not hungry.

275
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:23,214
I'm not cooking for you.

276
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:25,633
Who are you cooking for then?

277
00:15:26,717 --> 00:15:29,720
[soft music playing]

278
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:48,156
[thuds]

279
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:50,616
[sizzling]

280
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:06,174
[sizzles]

281
00:16:16,601 --> 00:16:19,604
[excite music playing]

282
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:36,287
[music continues]

283
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:37,538
[spoon clatters]

284
00:16:49,884 --> 00:16:50,676
[pot lid clatters]

285
00:16:50,801 --> 00:16:53,137
[mellow music playing]

286
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:01,145
[proud exclamation]

287
00:17:01,771 --> 00:17:02,647
[Chin-lai] Mom?

288
00:17:04,524 --> 00:17:06,526
Mom! I'm home!

289
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:08,861
Mom?

290
00:17:09,737 --> 00:17:10,613
I'm home!

291
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,160
- Mom?
- Grandma?

292
00:17:16,285 --> 00:17:17,328
- No.
- [door creaks open]

293
00:17:20,289 --> 00:17:22,749
- [Grandma] Ping?
- Mom. [laughs]

294
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:24,418
Jin-lai, you're here.

295
00:17:25,628 --> 00:17:27,170
[laughs]

296
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,714
Mom, I brought you
milkfish congee.

297
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:31,842
- [laughs]
- Oh.

298
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:37,264
Jin-lai?

299
00:17:37,265 --> 00:17:40,433
She's the mother
of my childhood friend, Ping.

300
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:41,518
Oh.

301
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:42,603
[Hsiu-wen] Uncle Jin-lai!

302
00:17:43,646 --> 00:17:45,731
- Hsiu-wen!
- [Hsiu-wen] Why are you here?

303
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:47,233
[Chin-lai]
I've been transferred back here.

304
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:49,819
[Hsiu-wen]
You're gonna make me
and Grandma fat!

305
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:52,445
[Chin-lai] Nonsense.
You're entering the college,
aren't you?

306
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:54,198
[Hsiu-wen] Yeah.

307
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:57,242
I'm working part-time to save up
for the tuition fees
and living expenses.

308
00:17:57,243 --> 00:17:58,744
[Chin-lai] Good. Go for it.

309
00:17:59,704 --> 00:18:00,746
I'll introduce someone.

310
00:18:02,248 --> 00:18:03,332
Come here!

311
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:06,627
Come! What's wrong?
My son, Lu-yung.

312
00:18:07,378 --> 00:18:09,714
[light music playing]

313
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:11,507
Hi.

314
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:17,262
- Nice to meet you.
You seem familiar.
- [bike bell rings]

315
00:18:17,263 --> 00:18:19,265
[chuckling]

316
00:18:21,392 --> 00:18:22,310
[Grandma] This is good.

317
00:18:24,312 --> 00:18:26,272
Eat more then.

318
00:18:27,398 --> 00:18:28,815
[Grandma] I'm on dialysis.

319
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:31,610
Food usually tastes bland.

320
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:33,403
They taste so bad.

321
00:18:33,404 --> 00:18:38,451
Only Jin-lai's food
from Chang Xin works for me.

322
00:18:38,576 --> 00:18:39,910
[Chin-lai laughs]

323
00:18:40,161 --> 00:18:42,788
There's plenty more.
Eat as much as you can.

324
00:18:46,876 --> 00:18:48,586
- Thank you, Uncle.
- [Chin-lai] What for?

325
00:18:48,711 --> 00:18:50,670
I cooked too much.

326
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:53,341
You're helping me finish it.
I should thank you.

327
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:59,429
[gentle music playing]

328
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:01,223
[chuckles]

329
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,573
Her illness seems
to be getting worse.

330
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:19,742
Yeah.

331
00:19:20,743 --> 00:19:23,746
Recently, she's started thinking
I'm her mom.

332
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:27,540
But that's fine.

333
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:29,627
Then she'll behave,
and it's easier
to make her happy.

334
00:19:30,586 --> 00:19:32,463
Right, my girl?

335
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:33,839
[Chin-lai chuckling]

336
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:38,302
I call her Mom,
and she calls you Mom.

337
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:39,804
Should I call you Grandma then?
[laughs]

338
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:41,846
Hi, my sweet boy.

339
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:43,849
[all laughing]

340
00:19:45,226 --> 00:19:47,687
Do you think there's something
weird with my son?

341
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:52,149
Yeah.

342
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:55,319
His personality.

343
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:00,282
You're right.

344
00:20:01,242 --> 00:20:03,285
[both laughing]

345
00:20:10,835 --> 00:20:11,669
What's wrong?

346
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:13,337
Nothing.

347
00:20:15,297 --> 00:20:19,218
I think you've become
who you wanted to be.

348
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:21,637
You too.

349
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:23,931
You own a restaurant now.

350
00:20:25,266 --> 00:20:26,684
It's not easy to do this
in Taipei City.

351
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:30,520
[sighs]
I barely have any customers.

352
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:31,480
Why?

353
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:35,651
Other than the first month,
we're just losing money.

354
00:20:38,404 --> 00:20:40,656
If you don't mind, I can look
through your accounts.

355
00:20:41,532 --> 00:20:42,949
I've done it.

356
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:43,951
The ratios are healthy.

357
00:20:44,702 --> 00:20:47,370
Rent's 13% of expenses.
Staff's at 20%.

358
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:48,497
Ingredients, 35%.

359
00:20:48,998 --> 00:20:51,959
Plus the supplier's a friend,
so prices are the lowest.

360
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:54,253
But if there's still room
to improve,

361
00:20:54,879 --> 00:20:56,422
I'd rather get
even better ingredients.

362
00:20:57,381 --> 00:20:59,258
Hm. [chuckles]

363
00:21:00,468 --> 00:21:01,343
What?

364
00:21:02,553 --> 00:21:04,013
Nothing.

365
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:08,893
I just feel
you've really changed.
You look like a boss.

366
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:13,981
By the way, I'm wondering...

367
00:21:14,565 --> 00:21:15,816
Are you marketing online?

368
00:21:16,692 --> 00:21:17,693
Yeah.

369
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:21,530
Ah, these photos...

370
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:25,034
really aren't very appealing.

371
00:21:25,910 --> 00:21:27,328
- Really?
- [chuckles]

372
00:21:27,912 --> 00:21:29,914
Get help
from a professional team.

373
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:34,084
The photos are ugly,
and the captions are too long.

374
00:21:34,335 --> 00:21:36,753
If you don't position yourself,
how are people
going to find you?

375
00:21:36,754 --> 00:21:39,089
Why should they dine
at your restaurant?

376
00:21:40,049 --> 00:21:40,925
Or...

377
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,428
I'm happy to help.

378
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:48,766
Okay.

379
00:21:50,601 --> 00:21:51,727
Then...

380
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:53,646
I've got to go.

381
00:21:57,399 --> 00:21:58,650
Are you hungry?

382
00:21:58,651 --> 00:22:00,569
Want some midnight snacks
at our restaurant?

383
00:22:01,946 --> 00:22:02,947
It's on me.

384
00:22:06,742 --> 00:22:07,618
Okay.

385
00:22:10,037 --> 00:22:10,913
Mm.

386
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:26,636
[dramatic music playing]

387
00:22:26,637 --> 00:22:28,639
[deep breaths]

388
00:22:32,643 --> 00:22:34,812
[indistinct chatter]

389
00:22:44,363 --> 00:22:45,698
[man laughs]

390
00:22:45,823 --> 00:22:48,158
[people chattering]

391
00:22:52,872 --> 00:22:55,416
[music continues]

392
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:11,682
[Hsiu-wen] What do you think?
How does it taste?

393
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:18,522
[jazz music playing]

394
00:23:18,647 --> 00:23:19,565
Impressive.

395
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,067
It's really good actually.

396
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:24,403
That's the answer
I've been waiting for.

397
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:30,451
But you look sad. Why?

398
00:23:35,706 --> 00:23:37,499
From our restaurant,
I can look up
and see this place.

399
00:23:40,210 --> 00:23:41,170
But from up here,

400
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:44,590
I can't see my Jin Lai Hao.

401
00:23:48,886 --> 00:23:50,471
Is this the distance between us?

402
00:23:55,643 --> 00:23:57,603
Just because this place is
on a higher floor,
don't you think?

403
00:23:57,728 --> 00:23:58,979
[both laugh softly]

404
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:08,530
If only Dad was around
to enjoy this view with us.

405
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:10,449
That would be nice.

406
00:24:12,785 --> 00:24:14,745
I really want
to defeat Chang Xin.

407
00:24:17,623 --> 00:24:19,499
No offense to you.

408
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:20,584
I know.

409
00:24:26,674 --> 00:24:28,050
To Uncle Jin-lai.

410
00:24:30,594 --> 00:24:31,553
To Dad.

411
00:24:41,188 --> 00:24:44,148
[gentle music playing]

412
00:24:44,149 --> 00:24:45,985
[sizzles]

413
00:24:49,822 --> 00:24:53,784
[singer] <i>♪ I'm building castles
Castles in the sand ♪</i>

414
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:57,955
<i>♪ With a bucket of water
I shaped them with my hands ♪</i>

415
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:02,126
<i>♪ I'm four years old
And I'm sat down with my dad ♪</i>

416
00:25:02,251 --> 00:25:04,962
<i>♪ Building castles in the sand ♪</i>

417
00:25:06,588 --> 00:25:07,798
<i>♪ I fly a kite... ♪</i>

418
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:09,008
[Lu-yung] Smells great.

419
00:25:09,133 --> 00:25:12,011
You're up.
Come, help me fry an egg.

420
00:25:12,803 --> 00:25:13,637
Okay.

421
00:25:14,930 --> 00:25:18,142
[singer] <i>♪ I'm five years old
It's the best time of my life ♪</i>

422
00:25:18,976 --> 00:25:21,520
<i>♪ Flying kite in the sky ♪</i>

423
00:25:22,855 --> 00:25:27,066
<i>♪ All I know
are these simple things ♪</i>

424
00:25:27,067 --> 00:25:31,195
<i>♪ My blue skies
and silver lining ♪</i>

425
00:25:31,196 --> 00:25:35,492
<i>♪ All that I have
is my sadness and joy ♪</i>

426
00:25:35,617 --> 00:25:38,746
<i>♪ Lucky I'm just a boy ♪</i>

427
00:25:42,833 --> 00:25:45,836
[music continues]

428
00:25:58,849 --> 00:25:59,850
Why such a good spread today?

429
00:26:00,559 --> 00:26:01,934
For our first day
of work and school,

430
00:26:01,935 --> 00:26:04,313
a hearty breakfast
to kick off the day right.

431
00:26:10,319 --> 00:26:12,863
Your fried egg isn't cooked
all the way.

432
00:26:16,325 --> 00:26:17,326
I think it's okay.

433
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:19,077
It's not browned enough.

434
00:26:19,078 --> 00:26:20,704
[chuckling]

435
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:23,332
You're in your old uniform.

436
00:26:25,709 --> 00:26:27,877
I'll buy a new one
at a nearby shop after school.

437
00:26:27,878 --> 00:26:29,088
No need.

438
00:26:29,213 --> 00:26:31,590
I'll pick you up after work.
We'll go together.

439
00:26:32,257 --> 00:26:33,217
Good idea.

440
00:26:45,604 --> 00:26:46,688
[music concludes]

441
00:26:50,234 --> 00:26:51,193
[Chien-yuan] Hi, beauty!

442
00:26:53,362 --> 00:26:54,238
Good morning.

443
00:26:55,823 --> 00:26:57,366
- Morning.
- Hey.

444
00:26:58,909 --> 00:27:00,160
Look at my license plate.

445
00:27:01,370 --> 00:27:04,123
What's there to see
on a license plate?
Please move your car.

446
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:07,125
Don't be so sure.

447
00:27:07,126 --> 00:27:08,961
- [sighs deeply]
- [engine shuts down]

448
00:27:09,086 --> 00:27:11,338
[Hsiu-wen] You can't park here.
The school bus is coming.

449
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:16,135
Come on.

450
00:27:16,260 --> 00:27:18,262
What? Let go.

451
00:27:18,387 --> 00:27:20,764
Let go. Let go.

452
00:27:21,557 --> 00:27:22,432
See?

453
00:27:25,185 --> 00:27:26,103
Your birthday.

454
00:27:29,231 --> 00:27:30,107
Hm.

455
00:27:31,984 --> 00:27:33,694
Come on. I'll give you a ride.

456
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:37,739
No, thanks. I'll take the bus.

457
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:42,661
Get in my car, okay?

458
00:27:42,786 --> 00:27:45,414
It's faster
and more comfortable.

459
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:47,874
And you can
avoid the crowds too. Right?

460
00:27:47,875 --> 00:27:48,791
[school bus honks]

461
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:50,419
Come on. What the hell?

462
00:27:51,295 --> 00:27:52,963
No, thanks. I'll take the bus.

463
00:27:53,088 --> 00:27:54,131
I love a crowded bus.

464
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:56,842
- Let me drive you, okay?
- Let go!

465
00:27:56,967 --> 00:27:58,010
Excuse me.

466
00:27:59,011 --> 00:27:59,845
The bus is here.

467
00:27:59,970 --> 00:28:01,138
[light music playing]

468
00:28:02,014 --> 00:28:02,890
Damn!

469
00:28:05,434 --> 00:28:06,768
See you later.

470
00:28:10,981 --> 00:28:11,899
[honks]

471
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,233
You bastard!

472
00:28:20,407 --> 00:28:22,408
- [Yu-jung] Hi, Chef.
- [Chin-lai] Hi, Yu-jung.

473
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:23,868
[Yu-jung]
How's the moving going?

474
00:28:23,869 --> 00:28:25,704
[Chin-lai] Quite well.
Lu-yung does everything.

475
00:28:26,205 --> 00:28:29,333
I think my daughter
should learn from your son.

476
00:28:30,125 --> 00:28:31,710
How's she?

477
00:28:31,835 --> 00:28:33,085
She's a first-grader.

478
00:28:33,086 --> 00:28:36,130
Let me tell you,
she's such a little devil.

479
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:38,508
Sometimes I feel like
I can't handle her.
So annoying.

480
00:28:38,759 --> 00:28:41,470
All kids are like that.
Get used to it. [laughs]

481
00:28:42,471 --> 00:28:46,057
By the way, did you know
the Meals for Elders
program here

482
00:28:46,058 --> 00:28:47,309
has been put on hold?

483
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:49,353
Put on hold?

484
00:28:51,355 --> 00:28:53,357
Why didn't Hsiu-wen tell me?

485
00:28:54,483 --> 00:28:55,442
Huh?

486
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:57,402
Nothing.

487
00:28:58,278 --> 00:29:02,406
Since it was my idea,
I'm wondering
why they haven't told me.

488
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:05,952
The chairman thinks
our charity work

489
00:29:05,953 --> 00:29:07,871
should be
more powerful and direct.

490
00:29:08,538 --> 00:29:10,749
He abandoned
those people halfway.

491
00:29:10,874 --> 00:29:12,167
How is that okay?

492
00:29:14,002 --> 00:29:16,964
Maybe I'll talk to the chairman.

493
00:29:17,798 --> 00:29:20,717
But I'm not sure
if he'll listen to me.

494
00:29:20,842 --> 00:29:21,760
It's alright.

495
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:25,097
He does everything
for the company's sake.

496
00:29:25,555 --> 00:29:27,224
Money should be spent wisely.

497
00:29:29,017 --> 00:29:31,853
[chuckles] Let's go to work.

498
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:39,236
[school bell chimes]

499
00:29:39,361 --> 00:29:41,238
[teacher] <i>We have
a transfer student today.</i>

500
00:29:41,363 --> 00:29:44,908
He has transferred to our school
because of his dad's job.

501
00:29:45,033 --> 00:29:46,450
We're all family here.

502
00:29:46,451 --> 00:29:48,078
Introduce yourself.

503
00:29:49,204 --> 00:29:50,414
Hi, I'm Chou Lu-yung.

504
00:29:52,082 --> 00:29:52,916
That's all?

505
00:29:55,043 --> 00:29:58,254
You can talk a little about
your ambitions and hobbies,

506
00:29:58,255 --> 00:30:00,132
so we'll understand you more.

507
00:30:01,133 --> 00:30:02,968
My dream is to get into
Central Police University.

508
00:30:03,093 --> 00:30:04,468
And I love jogging.

509
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:06,138
[low murmurs]

510
00:30:06,263 --> 00:30:10,100
[chuckles]
I think our new classmate
needs some time.

511
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:12,436
So, you'll sit
in that vacant seat.

512
00:30:12,561 --> 00:30:14,146
Hsiu-wen, raise your hand.

513
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:19,109
Right next to Hsiu-wen,
you'll sit there.

514
00:30:23,113 --> 00:30:25,948
Let's welcome our new classmate.

515
00:30:25,949 --> 00:30:27,200
[applause]

516
00:30:28,952 --> 00:30:30,287
Okay. That's it.

517
00:30:30,871 --> 00:30:33,874
Focus on your self-study.
No chatting.

518
00:30:51,975 --> 00:30:53,268
- [bully 1] Don't run.
- [thuds]

519
00:30:54,478 --> 00:30:55,979
[bully 2] Son of a bitch!

520
00:30:56,104 --> 00:30:58,065
- [bully 1] Stop running.
- [bully 2] Where are you going?

521
00:30:59,149 --> 00:31:00,233
Hey, sissy boy.

522
00:31:01,151 --> 00:31:03,027
This is a rose color

523
00:31:03,028 --> 00:31:04,279
that I've got
especially for you.

524
00:31:04,905 --> 00:31:06,073
It suits you well.

525
00:31:06,323 --> 00:31:08,200
[dramatic music playing]

526
00:31:08,325 --> 00:31:09,242
Stay still!

527
00:31:10,494 --> 00:31:13,455
Where are you going?
Let's make you look good.

528
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:15,581
Purse your lips. Come on. Do it.

529
00:31:15,582 --> 00:31:18,000
[laughing]

530
00:31:18,001 --> 00:31:19,544
Stay still. Stay the hell still!

531
00:31:23,173 --> 00:31:24,216
If you move again,

532
00:31:25,258 --> 00:31:26,343
I'll stick this up your asshole.

533
00:31:28,553 --> 00:31:30,472
Do you want makeup
or the other treatment?

534
00:31:31,515 --> 00:31:32,641
Make a choice.

535
00:31:33,642 --> 00:31:34,976
What? Silent?

536
00:31:35,602 --> 00:31:37,520
If you don't
make a choice, I will.

537
00:31:37,521 --> 00:31:39,272
[laughing]

538
00:31:41,316 --> 00:31:43,068
Makeup please.

539
00:31:44,236 --> 00:31:45,362
Makeup, yeah?

540
00:31:45,487 --> 00:31:46,905
Go on.

541
00:31:47,030 --> 00:31:48,198
Here we go.

542
00:31:50,992 --> 00:31:53,077
You look like a lady boy.
That's great!

543
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:54,413
[laughs]

544
00:31:55,622 --> 00:31:56,498
[Hsiu-wen] Ignore them.

545
00:31:58,291 --> 00:31:59,167
Why?

546
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:02,128
He's the son
of Chang Xin's boss.

547
00:32:02,129 --> 00:32:04,130
All the families here
either work for Chang Xin,

548
00:32:04,131 --> 00:32:05,631
or the kids are here
on their scholarships.

549
00:32:05,632 --> 00:32:08,051
- They're all supported
by the company.
- So?

550
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:11,303
Isn't your dad working
for Chang Xin too?

551
00:32:11,304 --> 00:32:12,472
Don't get him in trouble.

552
00:32:14,391 --> 00:32:16,143
[Chien-yuan] You're starting
to look like a drag queen.

553
00:32:22,858 --> 00:32:23,692
[Lu-yung] Hey.

554
00:32:26,278 --> 00:32:27,696
Stop it, okay?

555
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:31,700
So, we're in the same class.

556
00:32:34,703 --> 00:32:36,246
He wants to be a lady.

557
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:37,914
I'm helping him.

558
00:32:38,039 --> 00:32:39,291
What's wrong with that?

559
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:46,505
I'm putting on makeup for you.
What do you have to say?

560
00:32:46,506 --> 00:32:48,632
- Thank you very much.
- <i>Gracias</i> !

561
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:49,676
Thank you!

562
00:32:54,514 --> 00:32:56,600
Don't look at him. Look at me!

563
00:32:56,725 --> 00:32:58,101
What do you have to say?

564
00:33:00,103 --> 00:33:01,646
Thank you.

565
00:33:01,771 --> 00:33:03,231
[Chien-yuan] Louder.

566
00:33:04,441 --> 00:33:05,692
Come on!

567
00:33:06,485 --> 00:33:07,569
Say what?

568
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:10,112
Louder!

569
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:11,155
Thank you!

570
00:33:11,156 --> 00:33:12,490
[laughs]

571
00:33:12,491 --> 00:33:13,492
[bully 1] Good girl.

572
00:33:15,452 --> 00:33:16,536
[bully 2] You look pretty.

573
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:23,376
You're going too far.

574
00:33:26,296 --> 00:33:29,424
New kid, do you know who I am?

575
00:33:34,471 --> 00:33:35,805
[teacher] Come on, guys.

576
00:33:36,056 --> 00:33:37,140
Back to your seats.

577
00:33:38,808 --> 00:33:41,394
Back to your seats.
Stop messing around.

578
00:33:42,479 --> 00:33:45,315
Ma'am,
did you not see what they did?

579
00:33:50,153 --> 00:33:51,696
He's still right here.

580
00:33:54,741 --> 00:33:57,243
[teacher] What did I say?
Back to your seats now.

581
00:33:57,244 --> 00:33:59,662
Hurry up. All of you.

582
00:33:59,663 --> 00:34:01,205
Focus on your self-study.

583
00:34:01,206 --> 00:34:03,165
Will do. Thanks, ma'am!

584
00:34:03,166 --> 00:34:04,209
Thank you, ma'am!

585
00:34:11,716 --> 00:34:12,592
Yeah.

586
00:34:13,176 --> 00:34:14,135
That's it.

587
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:16,763
I am the school rules.

588
00:34:17,430 --> 00:34:18,390
Understand?

589
00:34:23,395 --> 00:34:24,521
- [teacher] Chien-yuen!
- [student] Oh, my!

590
00:34:24,646 --> 00:34:26,398
Chien-yuen? What are you doing?

591
00:34:26,523 --> 00:34:27,732
Chien-yuen?

592
00:34:28,858 --> 00:34:30,235
Chien-yuen?

593
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:32,070
Let me take a look.
Are you okay?

594
00:34:32,195 --> 00:34:33,612
Let me see.

595
00:34:33,613 --> 00:34:35,532
- [student] What the hell?
- [teacher] Come on, lemme check.

596
00:34:41,329 --> 00:34:42,414
Okay.

597
00:34:42,539 --> 00:34:44,498
Our VP Chiang here loves a joke.

598
00:34:44,499 --> 00:34:46,625
I'm still young and eager
to learn more.

599
00:34:46,626 --> 00:34:49,378
I'm just sharing my experience.

600
00:34:49,379 --> 00:34:50,755
But I meant it.

601
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:53,842
Chef Jin-lai is
not just a mentor
I respect very much,

602
00:34:54,092 --> 00:34:55,552
but also
one of Chang Xin's
founding members

603
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:57,053
and definitely an idol
to us all,

604
00:34:57,178 --> 00:34:58,680
- isn't he?
- [all] Yes!

605
00:34:59,389 --> 00:35:00,472
Chef is the man.

606
00:35:00,473 --> 00:35:01,725
Okay.

607
00:35:01,850 --> 00:35:05,227
Let's get down to business.

608
00:35:05,228 --> 00:35:09,273
Now, the most important part
of cooking is
the cooking oil you use.

609
00:35:09,274 --> 00:35:10,858
We at Chang Xin
have always upheld
high standards.

610
00:35:10,859 --> 00:35:13,570
We only use good oil
to show our respect
to the customers.

611
00:35:25,790 --> 00:35:27,083
What's wrong with the oil?

612
00:35:27,208 --> 00:35:28,668
Mr. Chairman requested for it.

613
00:35:47,604 --> 00:35:48,855
[laughs]

614
00:35:49,939 --> 00:35:51,441
We at Chang Xin

615
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:54,569
believe in always striving
for better.

616
00:35:55,195 --> 00:35:59,115
Today clearly they're testing
if I've lost my touch.

617
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:02,327
Thankfully,
my sense of smell is intact.

618
00:36:02,661 --> 00:36:06,915
This cooking oil here definitely
doesn't meet our standards.

619
00:36:09,793 --> 00:36:10,752
[Yu-jung] Excuse me.

620
00:36:11,628 --> 00:36:14,464
Chef, something's happened
to Lu-yung at school.

621
00:36:14,589 --> 00:36:16,841
It's complicated.
I'll catch you up on the way.

622
00:36:20,970 --> 00:36:22,514
[teacher] You think
you're great, don't you?

623
00:36:22,931 --> 00:36:24,640
Great at fighting?

624
00:36:24,641 --> 00:36:27,351
How dare you have guts to fight?

625
00:36:27,352 --> 00:36:28,520
[principal] You violent brute.

626
00:36:28,645 --> 00:36:30,146
I shouldn't have admitted you.

627
00:36:30,271 --> 00:36:31,439
Violence is unacceptable!

628
00:36:32,524 --> 00:36:33,817
[secretary] Mr. Chairman.

629
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:37,195
[dramatic music playing]

630
00:36:37,946 --> 00:36:40,156
- Hi, Mr. Principal.
- Hi, Mr. Chairman.

631
00:36:40,281 --> 00:36:42,367
Sorry for asking you
to come over.

632
00:36:43,660 --> 00:36:45,411
- [Chien-yuan] Dad.
- Don't worry.

633
00:36:45,412 --> 00:36:46,663
Just two kids playing around.

634
00:36:55,964 --> 00:36:57,298
You must be Chou Lu-yung.

635
00:37:02,762 --> 00:37:05,974
Mr. Chairman,
I didn't teach my son well.
I'm sorry.

636
00:37:06,224 --> 00:37:08,726
Damn! An employee's son
dares to hit me.

637
00:37:08,727 --> 00:37:10,019
Shut up.

638
00:37:17,444 --> 00:37:18,862
Sorry, Jin-lai.

639
00:37:19,487 --> 00:37:20,947
My son is a good-for-nothing.

640
00:37:22,031 --> 00:37:22,949
Mr. Principal?

641
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:25,785
[sighs]

642
00:37:26,619 --> 00:37:30,373
How does the school normally
deal with a situation like this?

643
00:37:31,374 --> 00:37:36,880
According to the school rules,
it's most likely expulsion.

644
00:37:39,674 --> 00:37:40,842
That serious?

645
00:37:41,885 --> 00:37:43,427
Mr. Principal,

646
00:37:43,428 --> 00:37:46,806
I've worked with Chef Chou
for many years.

647
00:37:47,390 --> 00:37:49,809
Without him, there would be
no Chang Xin as it is today.

648
00:37:50,518 --> 00:37:53,896
If the two boys agree
to reconcile,

649
00:37:53,897 --> 00:37:55,648
there's no need to go
as far as expulsion, right?

650
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:58,943
At your word, sir,

651
00:37:59,903 --> 00:38:01,738
we'll just give him a demerit.

652
00:38:01,863 --> 00:38:03,448
You're right.

653
00:38:03,573 --> 00:38:04,699
That would be all.

654
00:38:05,366 --> 00:38:06,701
We're all friends here.

655
00:38:07,786 --> 00:38:09,287
Here's the deal.

656
00:38:09,412 --> 00:38:12,040
Why don't you kneel down
and apologize to Chien-yuen?

657
00:38:12,791 --> 00:38:14,918
We'll accept it
like nothing's happened.

658
00:38:15,043 --> 00:38:16,419
Sounds good?

659
00:38:17,337 --> 00:38:19,005
[music continues]

660
00:38:25,637 --> 00:38:29,724
Jin-lai, it's a fact that
your son used violence.

661
00:38:30,558 --> 00:38:33,686
When our kids
do something wrong, aren't we
supposed to teach them?

662
00:38:34,646 --> 00:38:37,606
I also want to take this chance
to show my son that

663
00:38:37,607 --> 00:38:40,276
every action comes
with a consequence.

664
00:38:40,401 --> 00:38:41,903
Isn't this a good lesson
for the kids?

665
00:38:48,827 --> 00:38:51,621
[Lu-yung] Chang Chien-yuen
bullied a classmate.

666
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:53,081
The teacher chose
to turn a blind eye,

667
00:38:54,541 --> 00:38:55,874
and the principal chose
to allow it.

668
00:38:55,875 --> 00:38:58,544
What are you talking about?
I didn't bully anyone.

669
00:38:58,545 --> 00:39:02,131
Sir, you said every action
comes with a consequence.

670
00:39:03,967 --> 00:39:05,844
I'll accept my punishment.

671
00:39:05,969 --> 00:39:08,137
What about Chang Chien-yuen?
Is he getting punished?

672
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:11,307
My dad always says,

673
00:39:11,432 --> 00:39:14,644
what's right is right,
and what's wrong is wrong.

674
00:39:15,728 --> 00:39:18,648
We have to always hold on
to our beliefs.

675
00:39:19,732 --> 00:39:21,985
If I get expelled
for using violence,

676
00:39:22,110 --> 00:39:23,611
then Chang Chien-yuen
should too.

677
00:39:24,112 --> 00:39:26,364
It's you who used violence,
not me.

678
00:39:28,449 --> 00:39:31,661
I won't apologize to him
because I have nothing
to be sorry for.

679
00:39:37,125 --> 00:39:39,127
[laughs]

680
00:39:47,594 --> 00:39:48,678
Jin-lai,

681
00:39:49,762 --> 00:39:51,014
what do you think?

682
00:39:55,184 --> 00:39:56,935
I think,

683
00:39:56,936 --> 00:40:01,649
sir, I'm just an ordinary chef.

684
00:40:04,068 --> 00:40:06,529
I'm also wondering
how I've brought up
a son like him.

685
00:40:09,115 --> 00:40:10,825
But I think...

686
00:40:21,544 --> 00:40:23,046
my son is really amazing.

687
00:40:24,172 --> 00:40:26,674
[dramatic music playing]

688
00:40:32,055 --> 00:40:33,848
He just reminded me

689
00:40:35,808 --> 00:40:39,020
that we have to hold on
to our beliefs.

690
00:40:41,940 --> 00:40:44,859
I've just realized
how I've been astray

691
00:40:45,777 --> 00:40:48,529
from my own ideals lately.

692
00:40:52,075 --> 00:40:52,951
Sir,

693
00:40:54,994 --> 00:40:58,748
I think my son has done
a better job than I have.

694
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:04,962
[Chang Ta-chin]
Jin-lai, what you've said

695
00:41:04,963 --> 00:41:06,923
is telling me that you disagree
with my philosophy.

696
00:41:07,799 --> 00:41:11,010
How are we going
to keep working together?

697
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:16,766
I won't put you in a tough spot.

698
00:41:19,894 --> 00:41:21,479
I'll resign.

699
00:41:23,606 --> 00:41:25,233
Dad, this has nothing
to do with you.

700
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:33,783
Thank you for taking care
of me all these years, sir.

701
00:41:34,784 --> 00:41:35,952
Thank you.

702
00:41:45,628 --> 00:41:46,796
I see.

703
00:41:53,803 --> 00:41:55,596
[cries]

704
00:42:00,935 --> 00:42:03,688
Dad, I'm sorry.

705
00:42:07,817 --> 00:42:09,235
Don't say sorry.

706
00:42:10,236 --> 00:42:11,696
I should thank you instead

707
00:42:12,613 --> 00:42:14,282
for saving me money
by not having
to buy new uniforms.

708
00:42:18,161 --> 00:42:20,038
You've done nothing wrong.

709
00:42:20,955 --> 00:42:22,331
Why did you resign?

710
00:42:26,586 --> 00:42:27,962
Although I told you that

711
00:42:29,088 --> 00:42:31,841
we should start
with the end in mind,
hold on to our beliefs,

712
00:42:33,801 --> 00:42:35,303
I've actually failed to do it.

713
00:42:40,224 --> 00:42:42,643
But seeing how you were today,

714
00:42:44,020 --> 00:42:45,938
how you were holding on
to your beliefs,

715
00:42:48,858 --> 00:42:50,735
I'm so proud of you.

716
00:42:52,779 --> 00:42:54,238
[emotional music playing]

717
00:42:54,906 --> 00:42:57,909
My wish is for you
to keep living this way,

718
00:42:59,327 --> 00:43:03,372
so you can always
walk with your head held high.

719
00:43:08,878 --> 00:43:09,879
As for me,

720
00:43:11,172 --> 00:43:13,341
I've always wanted
to open a restaurant.

721
00:43:16,636 --> 00:43:18,137
You want to open a restaurant?

722
00:43:19,722 --> 00:43:21,557
Hey, I'm such a great cook

723
00:43:21,682 --> 00:43:23,975
that if I don't own
a place of my own,

724
00:43:23,976 --> 00:43:28,313
even God... won't tolerate it.

725
00:43:28,314 --> 00:43:30,316
[both laughing]

726
00:43:32,235 --> 00:43:33,111
Okay!

727
00:43:34,362 --> 00:43:35,821
Let's do it.

728
00:43:35,822 --> 00:43:37,073
We'll open a restaurant
of our own

729
00:43:37,740 --> 00:43:40,701
and cook our favorite dishes
with the best ingredients.

730
00:43:42,954 --> 00:43:43,955
Okay!

731
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:48,126
You've been 18 for a while.

732
00:43:49,210 --> 00:43:51,128
Have you been drinking
in secret?

733
00:43:51,129 --> 00:43:52,588
No.

734
00:43:52,713 --> 00:43:55,758
Good. So your first drink
will be with your dad.

735
00:43:57,969 --> 00:43:59,387
Bottoms up for me.
A sip for you.

736
00:44:08,187 --> 00:44:09,688
[sighs]

737
00:44:09,689 --> 00:44:11,022
Yeah.

738
00:44:11,023 --> 00:44:12,066
That's right.

739
00:44:13,276 --> 00:44:14,317
It tastes better.

740
00:44:14,318 --> 00:44:16,445
[laughing]

741
00:44:18,364 --> 00:44:19,824
How's the beer?

742
00:44:22,118 --> 00:44:23,995
- [clears throat]
- [laughs]

743
00:44:25,037 --> 00:44:25,913
It's sweet.

744
00:44:29,041 --> 00:44:31,210
That means you've had
a great day.

745
00:44:31,961 --> 00:44:33,963
Remember this taste.

746
00:44:36,215 --> 00:44:37,091
Yeah.

747
00:44:44,807 --> 00:44:45,641
[Chin-lai] Come on.

748
00:44:49,270 --> 00:44:50,897
[switch flips]

749
00:44:57,820 --> 00:44:59,154
Huh?

750
00:44:59,155 --> 00:45:00,740
What are you doing here?

751
00:45:01,115 --> 00:45:03,826
I've thought it through.
You will need me.

752
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:05,076
Huh?

753
00:45:05,077 --> 00:45:07,078
I'll be your restaurant manager.

754
00:45:07,079 --> 00:45:09,165
[light music playing]

755
00:45:14,045 --> 00:45:17,048
[credits music playing]
